Print a tree of documentation paths

Builds a directory-like tree from all page paths stored in the documentation
database.

Examples:
  snouty docs tree
  snouty docs tree --depth 2
  snouty docs tree -d 2
  snouty docs tree sdk

Add --json for machine-readable output. The tree prints as one JSON object,
{"children": [node, ...]}. Each node has name, the last segment of its path, and
path. A node has title when it is a page, and then `snouty docs show` accepts
its path. A node has children, sorted by name, when it has child nodes that
--depth did not remove. When no page matches, the output is {"children": []}:
  snouty --json docs tree sdk | jq -r '.. | .path? // empty'

Usage: snouty docs tree [OPTIONS] [FILTER]

Arguments:
  [FILTER]
          Optional case-insensitive filter applied to page paths and titles

Options:
  -d, --depth <DEPTH>
          Limit output to nodes at this depth or shallower

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --offline
          Don't check for documentation updates

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --utc
          Show times in UTC instead of the local timezone

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
